priority: -2

= The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> Have Peaked!

The rapid gains of the <span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">dynamic</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> movement, and the momentum that fueled them, have finally stalled. The once-united <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, held together by [+ royalist_leader +]'s principle of absolute leadership, is now suffering from internal conflicts as the party struggles to find a strategy to revitalize its once-<span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">dynamic</span> momentum. The industrial capitalist funders, their lower-middle-class base, their working-class crypto-<span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> left wing, and the revolutionary <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> are all turning against one another. The once-perfect arrangement is now unraveling.

We have observed that the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> are encountering clear ecological limits to their continued growth, particularly due to their inability to secure a decisive breakthrough into the Faithful or working-class voting blocs. This pattern has emerged across the Commonwealth, and with their adamant opposition to entering government without absolute power, they are destined to fizzle out.

- @nazi_explode: We must hold out, for at least a few more months.

@nazi_explode
on-arrival: knight_dissent -= 20; labor_dissent -= 10; left_dissent -= 10; center_dissent -= 10; reformist_dissent -= 10; ddp_left += 3; gold_left += 5; lvp_left += 5; ddp_cohesion += 3

The Unity system is not secure yet; we mustn’t become complacent. Anything could happen in the coming months. There are even rumors of an <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> coup, as a desperate last resort to seize power.